  "id": "Compound::DB01234 - Disease::DOID:8577",
  "verbalization": "Dexamethasone, Flumethasone Pivalate, and Betamethasone share a common structural relationship, all belonging to the class of 17-alpha-hydroxy steroid compounds and classified as therapeutic glucocorticoids. This shared pharmacological profile suggests a potential mechanism of action that may underlie their therapeutic effects. The evidence indicates that Dexamethasone, through its resemblance to Flumethasone Pivalate and Betamethasone, may exert a similar biological impact on the body, potentially modulating inflammatory processes. The observed relationship between Dexamethasone and Ulcerative Colitis is supported by the fact that Betamethasone, a closely related compound, is known to treat Ulcerative Colitis, implying a possible role for glucocorticoids in reducing inflammation. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of glucocorticoid receptor activation in the pathophysiology of Ulcerative Colitis, with Dexamethasone potentially offering a viable repurposing candidate due to its structural similarity and established therapeutic effects.",
